msgctxt "#31732"
msgid "Shows the round Add-ons icon.[CR]Where: Home screen, the corner bar."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#31733"
msgid "Shows the round Power icon, which opens the power menu.[CR]Where: Home screen, the corner bar."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#31734"
msgid "Shows a round Lists icon beside Favourites, whatever the main menu holds.[CR]Where: Home screen, the corner bar."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#31735"
msgid "Shows a round icon for the JellyStat Stats page, whatever the main menu holds.[CR]Where: Home screen, the corner bar."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#31736"
msgid "Draws no disc behind the round icons until one has focus. They still sit in the same place and still work.[CR]Where: Home screen, the corner bar."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#31737"
msgid "Cycles the accent colour used for focus highlights, headings and rules.[CR]Where: every screen of the skin."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#31738"
msgid "Opens Kodi's colour picker to choose any accent colour. Cancelling leaves the accent as it was.[CR]Where: every screen of the skin."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#31739"
msgid "Chooses the corner or edge where notifications and background progress bars appear.[CR]Where: pop up notifications, on any screen."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#31740"
msgid "Picks a theme by hand: Halloween, Devil's Night, Christmas, Christmas Eve or off.[CR]Where: the colours and seasonal scenery on every screen."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#31741"
msgid "Turns the Halloween theme on by itself from 29 to 31 October each year.[CR]Where: the colours and seasonal scenery on every screen."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#31742"
msgid "Turns the Christmas theme on by itself from the first Saturday of December to Boxing Day.[CR]Where: the colours and seasonal scenery on every screen."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#31743"
msgid "Writes a detailed skin log for fault finding, alongside Kodi's own log.[CR]Where: nothing on screen, a file named skin.functional-debug.log."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#31744"
msgid "Chooses the folder the debug log is written to.[CR]Where: nothing on screen, the debug log file."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#31745"
msgid "Puts the debug log back in Kodi's temp folder.[CR]Where: nothing on screen, the debug log file."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#31746"
msgid "Draws the active library filter state over the library lists, as a troubleshooting aid.[CR]Where: the video library screens."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#31747"
msgid "Takes a fresh copy of every skin setting now. A copy is also kept up to date by itself.[CR]Where: nothing on screen, the skin's own backup."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#31748"
msgid "Puts every skin setting back from the backup, after asking first. The skin then reloads.[CR]Where: every page of these settings."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#31749"
msgid "Sets the poster size in the gallery view: small, medium, large or extra large.[CR]Where: the video library screens, gallery view."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#31750"
msgid "Sets 11 or 12 columns for small posters. Use 11 if your TV crops the right edge.[CR]Where: the library gallery view, small size."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#31751"
msgid "Uses strict 2:3 posters, shorter than usual. Use it if your TV crops the bottom.[CR]Where: the video library screens, gallery view."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#31752"
msgid "Opens the press and hold menu at the left edge, or centred over the list.[CR]Where: the press and hold menu."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#31753"
msgid "Sets the order Movies always opens in, even after a genre filter.[CR]Where: the Movies library screen."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#31754"
msgid "Sets the direction of the Movies sort. Automatic is A to Z for Title and newest first for the rest.[CR]Where: the Movies library screen."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#31755"
msgid "Sets the order TV Shows always opens in, even after a genre filter.[CR]Where: the TV Shows library screen."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#31756"
msgid "Sets the direction of the TV Shows sort. Automatic is A to Z for Title and newest first for the rest.[CR]Where: the TV Shows library screen."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#31757"
msgid "Adds Collections and a row for each collection to the filters.[CR]Where: the library side menu, filter section."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#31758"
msgid "Puts the info bar for the focused title at the top of the screen instead of the bottom.[CR]Where: the library screens."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#31759"
msgid "Shows the genre of the focused title.[CR]Where: the library info bar."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#31760"
msgid "Shows the running time of the focused title.[CR]Where: the library info bar."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#31761"
msgid "Shows the star rating of the focused title.[CR]Where: the library info bar."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#31762"
msgid "Shows the age certificate of the focused title, such as PG or 12.[CR]Where: the library info bar."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#31763"
msgid "Shows the video resolution of the focused title, such as 4K or 1080p.[CR]Where: the library info bar."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#31764"
msgid "Shows how many years ago the focused title came out.[CR]Where: the library info bar."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#31765"
msgid "Shows when the focused title was last played.[CR]Where: the library info bar."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#31766"
msgid "Shows the time the focused title would finish if you started it now.[CR]Where: the library info bar."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#31767"
msgid "Shows how old the title is, in years, on the info screens. Titles under a year old show nothing.[CR]Where: the video info screen and the full screen info card."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#31768"
msgid "Sets what porting a list does to the current queue: clear it, keep it, or ask each time.[CR]Where: the Lists screen, when you port a list."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#31769"
msgid "Puts the action buttons in a band under the header instead of at the foot.[CR]Where: the Lists screen."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#31770"
msgid "Adds move up, move down and remove buttons to the focused item.[CR]Where: the Lists screen, the focused item row."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#31771"
msgid "Copies all your lists to a folder you choose, ready to import on another box.[CR]Where: nothing on screen, a lists.json file."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#31772"
msgid "Merges lists from a file exported on another box, matched by name. Nothing here is removed.[CR]Where: the Lists screen."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#31773"
msgid "Sets the filter the Favourites screen opens on: All, Movies, TV, Music, Apps or Other.[CR]Where: the Favourites screen."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#31774"
msgid "Sets the web address of your Radarr server.[CR]Where: nothing on screen, used by Remove from Radarr on the Lists screen."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#31775"
msgid "Sets Radarr's API key. It is kept in the skin's data folder and shown here only as Set or Not set.[CR]Where: nothing on screen."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#31776"
msgid "Chooses the one list that gets a Remove from Radarr button, or none.[CR]Where: the Lists screen, on that list."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#31777"
msgid "While on, Remove from Radarr removes nothing and only logs what it would have done.[CR]Where: the Radarr log."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#31778"
msgid "Asks Radarr whether the address and key work. It changes nothing.[CR]Where: a pop up notification."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#31779"
msgid "Shows the newest lines of the Radarr log, newest first.[CR]Where: a text window over these settings."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#31780"
msgid "Lets the JellyStat dashboard view and edit the skin's lists. It listens only on this box.[CR]Where: nothing on the TV, the lists in JellyStat's dashboard."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#31781"
msgid "Swaps the whole background setup at set times of day, with 2, 3 or 4 slots, or Off.[CR]Where: the background behind Home."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#31782"
msgid "Chooses which schedule slot the rows below are changing, and previews it.[CR]Where: the background behind Home."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#31783"
msgid "Sets when the slot being edited starts. It runs until the next slot starts.[CR]Where: the background behind Home."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#31784"
msgid "Chooses the background: off, a picture, recently watched, random from the library, a folder, or a genre.[CR]Where: the background behind Home."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#31785"
msgid "Picks the picture to use as the background.[CR]Where: the background behind Home."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#31786"
msgid "Removes the chosen background picture.[CR]Where: the background behind Home."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#31787"
msgid "Picks the folder for the slideshow: choose any picture in it and the whole folder is used.[CR]Where: the background behind Home."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#31788"
msgid "Chooses whether the genre slideshow draws on films, TV or both. Changing it clears the genre.[CR]Where: the background behind Home."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#31789"
msgid "Picks the genre the slideshow draws from.[CR]Where: the background behind Home."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#31790"
msgid "Draws only films never watched, and no TV, in random mode.[CR]Where: the background behind Home."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#31791"
msgid "Darkens the background so text on top stays readable.[CR]Where: the background behind Home."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#31792"
msgid "Draws the same background behind every screen, not just Home.[CR]Where: behind every screen of the skin."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#31793"
msgid "Darkens the background on screens other than Home, where lists sit on top of it.[CR]Where: behind every screen except Home."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#31794"
msgid "Keeps a playing video showing behind the menus when you leave the player.[CR]Where: behind every screen while video plays."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#31795"
msgid "Sets how long each picture stays before the slideshow moves on.[CR]Where: the background behind Home."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#31796"
msgid "Places the caption naming the current picture in a corner or bottom centre, or turns it off.[CR]Where: Home screen, over the background."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#31797"
msgid "Adds when the title was last watched after the caption.[CR]Where: Home screen, the background caption."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#31798"
msgid "Adds an Add To List button beside the caption.[CR]Where: Home screen, beside the background caption."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#31799"
msgid "Adds previous and next buttons for stepping through the slideshow by hand.[CR]Where: Home screen, the left and right edges."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#31800"
msgid "Puts the player controls at the top or bottom of the screen. Changing it reloads the skin.[CR]Where: the video player's on screen display and seek bar."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#31801"
msgid "Shows the poster of what is playing alongside the controls.[CR]Where: the video player's on screen display."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#31802"
msgid "Sets how much the video is darkened behind the settings dialogs opened while it plays.[CR]Where: the player's audio, video and subtitle settings."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#31803"
msgid "Shows how much of the video is buffered ahead.[CR]Where: the video player's on screen display and seek bar."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#31804"
msgid "Shows the Buffer All button. Off also puts buffering back to Kodi's defaults.[CR]Where: the video player's on screen display."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#31805"
msgid "Cycles the size of Kodi's playback buffer. Kodi uses about three times this in memory.[CR]Where: nothing on screen, every video Kodi plays."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#31806"
msgid "Cycles how fast Kodi fills the buffer, as a multiple of the video's bitrate, or adaptive.[CR]Where: nothing on screen, every video Kodi plays."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#31807"
msgid "Cycles what Kodi buffers: network shares and internet, internet streams only, everything, or nothing.[CR]Where: nothing on screen, every video Kodi plays."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#31808"
msgid "Puts all of Kodi's buffer settings back to their defaults.[CR]Where: nothing on screen, every video Kodi plays."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#31809"
msgid "Add-ons: settings for the add-ons Functional works with, JellyStat's figures under the stats and Engage's Coming up blocks on Home."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#31810"
msgid "Focus the Coming up list and press Down to scroll on through the next seven days, a day at a time. It goes back to the top when you move away.[CR]Where: Home screen, the Coming up list on the left."
msgstr ""
